We're planning on implementing HP DCE/9000 Version 1.1 on our G40.

Currently, one cell should suffice, but it seems like multiple cells will be necessary eventually.  With that in mind, ...

When you establish a peer-to-peer relationship between cells, an account is created in each cell with a unique UID and a shared password.  All principals from the foreign cell use the same account, so principals from the foreign cell lose their identity.

Based on that, it seems like one cell would be best, but how big can a cell get before performance becomes a problem?

beth


