Well, the gdad refers to underlying name resolution services to do it's job.
In the DNS world, this means, for instance, that if the named is not running on
the systems in the cell, then cdscp may be able to get to the gdad, but then
nothing happens.  Can you elaborate on the messages you get back from the 
cdscp show cell call?

