Hi!

I'm interested in your opinion to a specific aspect of DCE. The model of
threads implemented by DCE provides the programmer with the use of shared data
among all threads of one process. Also, the call of a remote procedure is, once
the procedure is written, very close to a local procedure call. But ( as far as
I know ) you can't use any global data (from the client's side) in a RP (on the
servers side) by means of shared memory of client and server. Wouldn't it be
nice to share data between different hosts? Until now, I think, in DCE this is
not possible at all. Yes, sure you can pass all needed data as parameters, but
it's just not the same. Also, sharing data by DFS or server queries can
certainly not replace using shared memory between client & server.

So, what do you think?

