>
>	Command "at".....
>	How to use it to run a scipt file just after I logout everytime???
>	Please e-mail to me to tell me...
>	Thanks you very much......
>	Bye...
>
>	William

This works, but not with "at", it is followed by an "at" example

make a program, and call it "delay"

% cat > delay
sleep $1
shift
$*
^D
% chmod +x delay

Then in your .logout:

% cat > .logout
delay 20 myscript &
^D

and so, when you logout, a background process will be started which
waits 20 seconds, and then runs your program, with all the parameters...
(none in this case)

I find "delay" to be a semi-useful program.

-----------------

The "at" cure

In your .logout

% cat > .logout
at now + 5 minutes my-script
^D


This I thjink is not as "nice"


