Either DEC's NSR or Legato's NetWorker. NSR is a repackaged Legato ( but
Legato don't yet have an OSF client/server instead you ned the dec one)

We are using a combination of Legato/NSR - Legato has more sensible
licensing, NSR works on more DEC systems. Legato will also back up all
your Novell systems ( and one day real soon now ) you Macs.

Works on either a Unix or PC server - we have one of each. And we love
it. We were doing all the unix backups automatically with local scripts
and 'clever' tricks, but Legato is a lot more complete. 

They hope to eventually offer a per useer archival function as well.



